# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else"), ch. 7 (the pattern binds the bundle's parts; `$m` follows `$k`), ch. 8 (`<-` binds the plain result) and ruling TC (places counted as built): loud gives 10 and `$k + 1`, so `@Wide 10` builds its label at 1 and gives 1, the next label is 2, the arm's label 3; soft gives 20 and `$k`, `@Wide 20` builds nothing and gives 2. A click moves `$k` and so `$m`. Never run: prismc refuses the program.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Label(text="ten")
    2: Ui.Label(text="wide 1 1")
    3: Ui.Label(text="loud")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="wide 1 2")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Label(text="wide 2 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="wide 2 1")
